Product Innovation Is Reshaping the Market
Manufacturers are developing surgical biomaterials with increasingly specialized characteristics.
Advanced Hydrogel Technologies
Hydrogels are used in selected surgical applications because their polymer structures can provide controlled physical properties.
Anti-Adhesion Gel Development
Adhesion barrier technologies are designed to address selected tissue separation requirements during healing.
Flowable Hemostatic Matrices
Flowable hemostatic materials can be applied to selected bleeding surfaces where their physical characteristics and approved indications are appropriate.
Polymer-Based Biomaterials
Synthetic polymers provide opportunities to develop materials with controlled composition and application properties.
Improved Delivery and Application Systems
Manufacturers are also focusing on product preparation, applicator design, and controlled material placement.
