Material expansion, swelling, and placement characteristics require careful evaluation.
Product Development Costs
Developing advanced biomaterials may involve extensive testing, manufacturing validation, and clinical evaluation.
Competition from Alternative Surgical Products
Spine surgery gels compete or coexist with other surgical adjuncts, including hemostatic materials, sealants, and tissue barriers.
Hospital Procurement Constraints
Healthcare providers must balance clinical requirements with product costs and purchasing policies.
Limited Application-Specific Evidence
Evidence supporting one surgical application cannot automatically be extended to other procedures or anatomical locations.
